      "extract": "To summarize, we can reproduce the whole collection of the single-Schur sums from [@Mac secs.1.5,3.4,3.5]. They are naturally divided in three blocks, and the formulas are given also in terms of symmetric variables $x_i$ such that $p_k=\\sum_ix_i^k$. **1.** The first one is already familiar $$\\begin{aligned} \\label{1} \\sum_RS_R=\\prod_i{1\\over 1-x_i}\\prod_{i<j}{1\\over 1-x_ix_j} = \\exp\\left\\{\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty",
