      ],
      "extract": "As we saw in the previous sections, the Schur functions form a full set of polynomials that have simple averages, this phenomenon is called superintegrability [@MMsi]. Similarly, one can construct a full set of *bilinear* combinations with simple averages too. This phenomenon is called strong superintegrability, and first we remind how this phenomenon looks like in the case of the Gaussian Hermitian matrix model.",
